`check_constant_columns` flags a numeric column when it holds two or more values, all equal, for arrays and tables alike. It tested for a standard deviation of exactly zero, which misses constant floats such as three copies of `0.1` (their computed spread is 1.4e-17). Its array and table paths also disagreed: an array flagged a single row, or one value among NaNs, as constant and a table did not, and an all-NaN array column raised a `RuntimeWarning`. Array findings now name the columns by position, as table findings name them, and the check is faster: 0.13-0.21 s instead of 0.31-0.62 s on a 49,155 x 2,048 array.
